{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370751-branch-of-the-divine-tempest-3-dot-artifact-evocations-feedback-requested","id":1370751,"title":"Branch of the Divine Tempest (3-dot artifact + evocations, feedback requested)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-27T07:09:47-08:00","id":1370751,"title":"Branch of the Divine Tempest (3-dot artifact + evocations, feedback requested)","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Branch of the Divine Tempest</b></span><br /> <b>(Soulsteel Wrackstaff, Artifact ***)</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Initially appearing to be a gnarled wood staff, on closer inspection the Branch is made of metal-- layers of bronze and iron twisted together around a core of pure soulsteel. Breath of Two Wind's titular breath has stirred the ghosts captured within to new life, and their revitalized spirits course through the staff. It bends and twists slightly even when sitting still, and weighs nowhere near as much as it ought to. When dropped, it takes several seconds to reach the ground.<ul><li><b>Attunement</b>: 5m</li> <li><b>Type</b>: Medium (+3 ACC, +12 DMG, +1 DEF, OVW 4)</li> <li><b>Tags</b>: Bashing, Melee</li> <li><b>Hearthstone Slot(s)</b>: 1</li> <li><b>Era</b>: Time of Troubles</li> </ul><br /> <b>EVOCATIONS</b><br /> The Branch's shape changes constantly as the spirits within twist and turn, but a determined wielder can order them into a new configuration. Once per round as a reflexive action, she may add, remove, or change one weapon tag for the duration of the scene.<br /> <br /> The Branch can have up to five tags simultaneously. One of these must specify the damage type (Bashing or Lethal), and another must specify the ability used (Brawl, Martial Arts, or Melee). The Natural tag cannot be selected.<br /> <br /> <b>Special: </b>To be Resonant with the Branch, the wielder must know the Divine Wind Animation thaumaturgy. If they do not, they are considered Dissonant.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Divine Wind Animation (***)</i></b><i>: The thaumaturge's soul overflows the bounds of their mortal form, surging forth at the slightest provocation. As an action, she may expend 2m or 1wp to breathe life into an object no larger than a five foot cube. Until the end of the round, the object may move about on its own, its shape changing if necessary to accommodate that motion. The animated object obeys the desires of the thaumaturge, and is incapable of undertaking any action that requires a check.</i><br /> <br /> <i>As a special case, the thaumaturge can breathe life into a weapon and send it winging towards a foe. Doing so requires a weapon weighing no more than five pounds, and uses (Perception + Occult) for the attack roll. Animated weapons have the traits of medium mundane weapons, with the Throwing (Short) tag, as well as any others appropriate for the specific weapon being animated.</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The thematics on this are a little wonky, but the character in question has had this power from the start of the campaign; it's sorta her trademark. Mechanical tweaks are possible, replacement is not)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>ENDLESS PANOPLY PRANA </b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> The bounty of the Branch extends beyond mere blades and spears. As a simple action, its wielder can cause the staff to produce one piece of exceptional equipment weighing less than five pounds. At the end of the scene, the tool melts away into vapor.<br /> <br /> <b>IRON LOTUS UNFURLS</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Resonant<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> <br /> When using a Shape Sorcery action, the Branch's wielder may channel sorcerous motes into the artifact, charging it with power. For every two sorcerous motes spent this way, the Branch grows one weapon with any tags you desire. Until it successfully strikes an enemy-- or until the end of the scene, whichever comes first-- the weapon uses the statistics of a light artifact weapon. Afterwards, they melt away into vapor.<br /> <br /> <b>Resonant</b>: The weapons take flight and circle around the wielder for the duration of the scene. As an attack action, she may send one flying at a foe. This functions as the Divine Wind Animation thaumaturgy, save that the weapon's range is extended to long.<br /> <br /> <b>HURRICANE MEDITATION TECHNIQUE</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 3m <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Resonant<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Iron Lotus Unfurls<br /> <br /> Power flows two ways. Just as sorcerous power may be channeled into the Branch, so too can it travel from Branch to sorcerer. When attacking with the Branch, she can spend currently banked sorcerous motes to add dice to your attack roll or to the raw damage of a withering attack. She may spend a maximum of number of sorcerous motes equal to her Intelligence, divided between the two categories however she chooses.<br /> <br /> <b>Resonant</b>: The wielder adds her Essence to the maximum number of sorcerous motes she can commit, and may use this Evocation to supplement ranged attacks made using Iron Lotus Unfurls.<br /> <br /> <b>CHAINS UPON THE BREEZE</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 3m, 1wp <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Resonant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Iron Lotus Unfurls<br /> This Evocation supplements a gambit performed using the Branch, granting double 10s on the Initiative roll.<br /> <br /> <b>GALE-FORCE STRIKE</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 7m <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-only<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Hurricane Meditation Technique<br /> <br /> After using the Branch as a melee weapon to make a successful decisive attack, or a withering attack that deals at least five points of damage, the wielder may activate this Charm to knock the target prone. In addition, she can convert banked sorcerous motes to raw kinetic force.<br /> <br /> If she converts at least two sorcerous motes, the opponent is lifted and bodily hurled into an object or surface within close range, hitting it with an impact equivalent to falling a short distance (see falling damage, p. 232), destroying any less-obdurate objects he collides with, such as wooden furniture.<br /> <br /> If she converts at least five sorcerous motes, the foe is knocked into an object at close range with tremendous force, or is sent sailing a remarkable distance by the force of the blow. If the former, the opponent hits a surface with force sufficient to leave cracks in a stone wall, impacting with a surface as if he had fallen from a medium distance. If the latter, the force of the blow throws him to short range with a short-distance falling impact.<br /> <br /> If she converts at least ten sorcerous motes, the foe is thrown to short range and suffers an impact like falling from a medium height.<br /> <br /> <b>WIND FUELS THE TREES</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4m, 1wp <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Uniform<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Hurricane Meditation Technique<br /> <br /> This Evocation can be used to flurry an attack made using the Branch with a Shape Sorcery action. It may be used only once per scene, unless reset by rolling three or more 10s on a Shape Sorcery action.<br /> <br /> <b>INVOCATION OF DRIFTING STEEL</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m, 1wp <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Dissonant, Decisive-only<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Chains Upon the Breeze<br /> <br /> After animating multiple weapons with Iron Lotus Unfurls, you may split your Initiative to make a series of up to (1/2 Intelligence, rounded up) decisive attacks. These attacks may be directed at a single target, or multiple targets as the player desires. The player divides the Solar\u2019s Initiative between the attacks when they activate the Charm, for the purpose of determining the damage of each attack. Each attack must have at least one Initiative allocated to it, and unlike normal decisive attack resolution, the Solar does not return to base Initiative until the final attack is resolved, and only loses Initiative for missed attacks if all of her attacks fail to connect. In the case of such a miss, the Exalt loses two Initiative per attack attempted.<br /> <br /> <b>Dissonant</b>: Wielders who are dissonant with the Branch cannot awaken this Evocation<br /> <br /> <b>WIND THAT BREAKS THE WORLD</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m, 1wp, 3a <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Dissonant, Dual<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Invocation of Drifting Steel<br /> <br /> Channeling the full power of your anima into your animated weapons, you may make one attack with each weapon animated by Iron Lotus Unfurls, to a maximum of your Intelligence. These attacks may be withering, decisive, or alternating however you choose.<br /> <br /> <b>Dissonant</b>: Wielders who are dissonant with the Branch cannot awaken this Evocation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 02-27-2020, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}